<p>This draft describes proposed terms for using the Lumora e-commerce marketplace. It is provided for review and does not replace a final agreement approved by Lumora.</p>

<h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
<p>By creating an account or using Lumora, you confirm that you have read this draft and agree to the final User Agreement when it is published. If you do not agree to the final terms, do not create or continue using an account.</p>

<h2>2. Account Registration</h2>
<p>Provide information that is accurate and current, including the information needed to create and operate your account. You must meet the age requirement shown during registration. Keep your account information up to date and do not impersonate another person or create an account using information you are not authorized to use.</p>

<h2>3. User Responsibilities</h2>
<p>Use Lumora lawfully and respectfully. You are responsible for activity carried out through your account, for the accuracy of information you submit, and for following applicable laws and the marketplace policies shown to you.</p>

<h2>4. Account Security</h2>
<p>Keep your password and verification codes confidential. Notify Lumora through its published support channel if you believe someone has accessed your account without permission. Do not share access to an account in a way that compromises its security.</p>

<h2>5. Orders and Transactions</h2>
<p>Product listings, prices, availability, order acceptance, delivery, cancellations, returns, and refunds are subject to the information shown at checkout and the applicable marketplace policies. A seller is responsible for the accuracy of its listing and fulfillment obligations. The final agreement should describe Lumora's and sellers' respective responsibilities, payment flows, and dispute process.</p>

<h2>6. Prohibited Activities</h2>
<p>Do not use Lumora to break the law, commit fraud, interfere with the service, bypass security, submit false information, infringe another person's rights, manipulate reviews or transactions, or list or transact in items prohibited by law or Lumora's published policies.</p>

<h2>7. Account Suspension and Termination</h2>
<p>The final agreement should explain the circumstances and process for restricting, suspending, or closing an account, including notice, review, and any steps available to contest a decision. This draft does not establish a finalized enforcement procedure.</p>

<h2>8. Changes to the Agreement</h2>
<p>Lumora should publish material changes with an updated version and effective date and explain when renewed acceptance is required. Continued use should not be treated as acceptance where applicable law requires another form of notice or consent.</p>

<h2>9. Contact and Review</h2>
<p>Lumora's legal name, governing terms, support contact, and dispute process have not been supplied in this draft. These details must be verified and added before publication.</p>
